{"id":"h4-05-q3","title":"Stream processing and backpressure","scopeHtml":"<p>Scope: windows, watermarks, lag, DLQ and retries. Questions are still to be written.</p>","notes":[{"id":"what-stream-processing-is","title":"What stream processing is","html":"<p><strong>Stream processing computes results continuously as events arrive, instead of waiting to run a batch job on yesterday's data.</strong> Examples: fraud score in 200 ms, a live dashboard of orders per minute, ETA updates.</p>\n<p>Typical stack: Kafka as the source, a processor (Kafka Streams, Apache Flink, Spark Structured Streaming), state held locally (RocksDB) and checkpointed, results written to Kafka, a DB or a cache.</p>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 488.79999999999995 130\" width=\"488.79999999999995\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Events flow through a processor that keeps state\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M115.2 65 L171.2 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M115.2 65 L171.2 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M310.4 65 L366.4 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M310.4 65 L366.4 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M310.4 65 L366.4 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M310.4 65 L366.4 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"43\" width=\"103.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"63.6\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Kafka topic</text><rect x=\"171.2\" y=\"43\" width=\"139.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"240.79999999999998\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Stream processor</text><rect x=\"366.4\" y=\"12\" width=\"110.4\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"421.59999999999997\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">State store</text><rect x=\"366.4\" y=\"74\" width=\"110.4\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"421.59999999999997\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Output topic</text></svg><figcaption>Events flow through a processor that keeps state</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Worked example.</strong> Count orders per city per minute from 5,000 events/s. State is a map of (city, minute) to count: say 500 cities x a few open windows, a few thousand entries, tiny. The hard part is not memory but late and out-of-order events.</p>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> Uber (Flink for surge and marketplace metrics), Netflix (Flink pipelines), LinkedIn (Samza and Kafka Streams), Alibaba (Flink for Singles' Day dashboards).</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> A toll-booth counter that updates the total after every car, instead of counting tickets at midnight.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Proposing streaming where an hourly batch is enough; streaming costs more to operate.</li>\n<li>Ignoring state: where it lives, how big, how it recovers.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"windows","title":"Windows","html":"<p><strong>A window groups an unbounded stream into finite chunks you can aggregate.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Tumbling:</strong> fixed, non-overlapping (00:00 to 00:01, 00:01 to 00:02).</li>\n<li><strong>Sliding (hopping):</strong> fixed size, moves by a smaller step (5-minute window every 1 minute); each event lands in several windows.</li>\n<li><strong>Session:</strong> closes after a gap of inactivity (for example 30 minutes without a click); length varies per user.</li>\n</ul>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span>Tumbling 1 min:  [0-1)[1-2)[2-3)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>Sliding 3m/1m:   [0-3)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>                   [1-4)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>                     [2-5)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>Session gap 5m:  click click   (gap)   click click click</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>                 |--session 1--|        |---session 2---|</span></span></code></pre>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 594 68\" width=\"594\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Events are assigned to windows by event time\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M102 34 L158 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 34 L158 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;0.251;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M290 34 L346 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M290 34 L346 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M436 34 L492 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M436 34 L492 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;0.751;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Events</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"12\" width=\"132\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"224\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Window assigner</text><rect x=\"346\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"391\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Aggregate</text><rect x=\"492\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"537\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Result</text></svg><figcaption>Events are assigned to windows by event time</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Worked example.</strong> Sliding 5-minute window every 1 minute over 10,000 events/s: each event is in 5 windows, so aggregation work multiplies by 5. Flink optimises this with panes or incremental aggregation.</p>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> Sessionisation of user activity (Spotify, e-commerce analytics), per-minute metrics (Datadog-style), anomaly detection with sliding windows.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> Counting traffic per hour (tumbling), \"last 60 minutes, updated each minute\" (sliding), or one visit to a shop from entering to leaving (session).</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Using processing time when business correctness needs event time.</li>\n<li>Large sliding windows with tiny steps, which multiplies compute and state.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"event-time-watermarks-and-late-data","title":"Event time, watermarks and late data","html":"<p><strong>Event time is when the thing happened (a timestamp from the phone). Processing time is when the system saw it.</strong> Mobile events arrive late: a user goes through a tunnel and the click arrives 3 minutes after it happened.</p>\n<p><strong>A watermark is the processor's claim \"I believe no events older than time T will arrive any more\".</strong> When the watermark passes the end of a window, the window fires. Typical rule: <code>watermark = max event time seen - allowed lateness bound</code> (for example 10 s).</p>\n<p>Trade-off: a long delay gives correct results but high latency; a short delay gives fast results but drops or corrects late events. Options for later arrivals: drop, send to a side output, or allow <code>allowedLateness</code> and emit an updated result.</p>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 643.2 130\" width=\"643.2\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Watermark decides when a window closes\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M102 65 L158 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 65 L158 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;0.251;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M318.8 34 L374.8 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M318.8 34 L374.8 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M485.20000000000005 34 L541.2 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M485.20000000000005 34 L541.2 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;0.751;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M102 65 L158 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 65 L158 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;0.251;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M318.8 96 L374.8 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M318.8 96 L374.8 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"43\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Events</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"12\" width=\"160.8\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"238.4\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Watermark generator</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"74\" width=\"160.8\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"238.4\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Late event</text><rect x=\"374.8\" y=\"12\" width=\"110.4\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"430\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Window fires</text><rect x=\"374.8\" y=\"74\" width=\"110.4\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"430\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Side output</text><rect x=\"541.2\" y=\"43\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"586.2\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Output</text></svg><figcaption>Watermark decides when a window closes</figcaption></figure>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\"># Flink-style idea (PyFlink-like pseudocode)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">stream.assign_timestamps_and_watermarks(</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">    WatermarkStrategy.for_bounded_out_of_orderness(Duration.ofSeconds(</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">10</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">)))</span></span></code></pre>\n<p><strong>Worked example.</strong> Window 12:00 to 12:01, watermark lag 10 s. The window fires when an event with time 12:01:10 is seen. A click stamped 12:00:30 arriving at 12:01:20 is late: handled by allowed lateness (update) or side output.</p>\n<p><strong>Gravity.</strong> The watermark bound is a tunable choice you can revisit, but changing it changes output semantics (and results already emitted). Idle partitions can stall watermarks; use idleness timeouts.</p>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> Google Dataflow/Beam model (the paper \"The Dataflow Model\") introduced this language; Flink implements it.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> Closing exam submissions: you wait a few minutes after the deadline for students stuck in the queue, then stop.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Confusing watermark with the current time.</li>\n<li>One idle partition holding back the global watermark.</li>\n<li>Dropping late data silently with no metric.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"consumer-lag-and-backpressure","title":"Consumer lag and backpressure","html":"<p><strong>Consumer lag = how many messages (or seconds) the consumer is behind the producer.</strong> It is the most important health number for a streaming system. Rising lag means consumers are slower than producers.</p>\n<p><strong>Backpressure is the system slowing producers or upstream stages because a downstream stage cannot keep up.</strong> In Kafka the log itself is the buffer, so producers are never blocked by slow consumers: lag just grows (until retention deletes data you have not read!). In Flink, bounded network buffers propagate backpressure upstream to the source, which then reads slower.</p>\n<p>Handling rising lag:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Check if it is a sudden spike (burst) or a trend.</li>\n<li>Scale consumers up to the partition count.</li>\n<li>Fix the slow part (DB calls per message; batch them; async I/O).</li>\n<li>Increase partitions if consumers already equal partitions.</li>\n<li>Shed or sample low-value work.</li>\n</ol>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 526 68\" width=\"526\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Lag grows when consumers are slower than producers\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M165.6 34 L221.6 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M165.6 34 L221.6 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M311.6 34 L367.6 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M311.6 34 L367.6 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"12\" width=\"153.6\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"88.8\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Producer 10k per s</text><rect x=\"221.6\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"266.6\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Kafka</text><rect x=\"367.6\" y=\"12\" width=\"146.4\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"440.8\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Consumer 6k per s</text></svg><figcaption>Lag grows when consumers are slower than producers</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Worked example.</strong> Produce 10,000 msg/s, consume 6,000 msg/s: lag grows 4,000/s = 14.4M per hour. With 7-day retention you have time, but with 1-hour retention you would lose data after about 1 hour. Alert on lag in <strong>time</strong> (<code>lag / consume rate</code>) and on the lag growth rate, not just absolute count.</p>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> Tools: Burrow (LinkedIn), Kafka Lag Exporter, Confluent Control Center, CloudWatch for MSK. Uber and others alert on end-to-end latency using event timestamps.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> A sink with the tap on faster than the drain: the water level (lag) rises, and when it overflows (retention) you lose water.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Assuming Kafka pushes back on producers; it does not, it buffers.</li>\n<li>Scaling consumers beyond partition count.</li>\n<li>Alerting only on absolute lag, which is meaningless at different rates.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"retries-dead-letter-queues-and-poison-messages","title":"Retries, dead-letter queues and poison messages","html":"<p><strong>Some messages fail: transient (DB down) or permanent (bad data, a \"poison pill\").</strong> Retrying a permanent failure blocks the partition forever, since Kafka consumers process in order.</p>\n<p>Pattern:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Retry transient errors a few times with <strong>exponential backoff</strong> (for example 1 s, 5 s, 30 s) and jitter.</li>\n<li>After N attempts, publish the message plus error info (original topic, partition, offset, exception) to a <strong>dead-letter topic/queue</strong> and <strong>commit and move on</strong>.</li>\n<li>Alert on DLQ depth; fix the bug; replay from the DLQ.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>For ordered streams, non-blocking retries use separate <strong>retry topics</strong> (<code>orders.retry.1m</code>, <code>orders.retry.10m</code>) so the main partition keeps flowing, at the cost of reordering.</p>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 780.8 68\" width=\"780.8\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Failed messages go to retry tiers, then the DLQ\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M108 34 L164 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M108 34 L164 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.200;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.200;0.201;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M254 34 L310 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M254 34 L310 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.200;0.400;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.200;0.400;0.401;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M434.8 34 L490.8 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M434.8 34 L490.8 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.400;0.600;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.400;0.600;0.601;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M622.8 34 L678.8 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M622.8 34 L678.8 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.600;0.800;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.600;0.800;0.801;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"12\" width=\"96\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"60\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Main topic</text><rect x=\"164\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"209\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Consumer</text><rect x=\"310\" y=\"12\" width=\"124.8\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"372.4\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Retry topic 1m</text><rect x=\"490.8\" y=\"12\" width=\"132\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"556.8\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Retry topic 10m</text><rect x=\"678.8\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"723.8\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">DLQ</text></svg><figcaption>Failed messages go to retry tiers, then the DLQ</figcaption></figure>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\"># Spring Kafka style idea</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#22863A;--shiki-dark:#85E89D\">retry</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: { </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#22863A;--shiki-dark:#85E89D\">attempts</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">4</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#22863A;--shiki-dark:#85E89D\">backoff</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: { </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#22863A;--shiki-dark:#85E89D\">initial</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">1s</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#22863A;--shiki-dark:#85E89D\">multiplier</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">5</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#22863A;--shiki-dark:#85E89D\">max</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">60s</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> } }</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#22863A;--shiki-dark:#85E89D\">dead-letter-topic</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">orders.dlq</span></span></code></pre>\n<p><strong>Worked example.</strong> One malformed JSON message at offset 8,421 throws on every attempt. With infinite retry, 3 million later messages are stuck behind it and lag explodes. After 3 attempts it goes to <code>orders.dlq</code> and consumption continues; on-call fixes the parser and replays 1 message.</p>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> Uber's blog on reliable reprocessing with retry topics and DLQs; SQS has native DLQs via <code>maxReceiveCount</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> A parcel with a wrong address goes into a \"problem\" bin instead of blocking the conveyor belt.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Infinite retry loops and head-of-line blocking.</li>\n<li>A DLQ nobody monitors; it becomes a data graveyard.</li>\n<li>Retrying without idempotency, so a side effect happens twice.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"summary","title":"Summary","html":"<ul>\n<li>Stream processing = continuous computation with local, checkpointed state (Flink, Kafka Streams).</li>\n<li>Windows: tumbling, sliding, session; sliding multiplies work.</li>\n<li>Use event time with watermarks; the bound trades latency vs completeness; handle late data explicitly.</li>\n<li>Lag (best in seconds) is the health metric; Kafka buffers instead of blocking producers; scale to partition count, then fix the handler.</li>\n<li>Retry with backoff, then DLQ; use retry topics to avoid blocking; always monitor the DLQ.</li>\n</ul>"}],"questions":[]}